/target
crates/*/target
# `ref_data/` is NOT ignored: a test fixture nobody can regenerate is not a
# reproducibility claim. burn-gdn2's oracle fixtures are committed (the
# exceptions below) and burn-sct's is wanted the same way once its generator
# exists — see crates/burn-gdn2/TEST-AUDIT.md.
**/*.bin
# The f64 reference fixtures, same reason and one more: `tests/ref_f64.rs` must
# run in CI without Python or NumPy present at all, so the expected values have
# to be bytes in the tree. `ref_f64.bin` is the 18-case length matrix;
# `ref_f64_faults.bin` is the other side of its margin, and a margin asserted
# against data nobody can regenerate is not a margin; `ref_f64_broad.bin` is the
# 1000-case breadth sweep behind `oracle_breadth`/`oracle_chunk`.
#
# MEASURED 2026-09-29, and this is why the last exception exists: writing
# `ref_f64_broad.bin`, writing the two tests against it, and getting them green
# all worked while `git status` did not list the file — `**/*.bin` was the only
# reason. A fixture that is not in the tree is a test that does not exist for
# every reader but the one who ran the generator, and nothing local complains:
# the `include_bytes!` resolves on the author's disk. `git check-ignore -v <new
# fixture>` before trusting a green run.
!crates/burn-gdn2/tests/ref_f64.bin
!crates/burn-gdn2/tests/ref_f64_faults.bin
!crates/burn-gdn2/tests/ref_f64_broad.bin
# The f64 GRADIENT oracle for the chunked-WY backward, same reason: its
# expected values come from NumPy, and `tests/autodiff_bwd_f64.rs` must run in
# CI with no Python present. `ref_bwd_f64.bin` is the oracle;
# `ref_bwd_f64_faults.bin` is the other side of its margin; and
# `ref_bwd_f64_carry.bin` is the ORACLE FOR THE STATE-CARRY DEFECT below, so
# the diagnosis carries its own expected values rather than only a number in
# a commit message.
!crates/burn-gdn2/tests/ref_bwd_f64.bin
!crates/burn-gdn2/tests/ref_bwd_f64_faults.bin
!crates/burn-gdn2/tests/ref_bwd_f64_carry.bin
Cargo.lock.bak
.bulba/

# The oracle fixtures ARE the tier-(a) artifacts - always tracked,
# whatever pattern above matches them.
!crates/*/tests/**/*.bin
